# default.pgo capture manifest

Regenerate with `make pgo-regenerate` (which runs scripts/pgo-regenerate.sh),
or by hand with the procedure in sdk/docs/architecture.md, "Build Profiles and
Observable Runtime". Update this file in the same change set as default.pgo.

    revision:   0d1b91b3 + uncommitted runtime performance programme
    toolchain:  go1.26.4 linux/amd64
    host CPU:   Intel(R) Xeon(R) W-11955M CPU @ 2.60GHz
    captured:   2026-07-24
    capture:    IE_CPUPROFILE=<path> on a `go build -pgo=off` binary
    merge:      go tool pprof -proto <profiles...> > default.pgo

Captured after the runtime performance programme's structural changes
(compositor unchanged-frame skip, retained hardware-compositor layers, the
Voodoo one-submit/persistent-map/async-present present path), which shifted the
amd64 hot paths. Total samples 131.77 s over 169.72 s wall (77.6 %).

## Per-target profiles

`default.pgo` is the amd64 profile. The Makefile passes -pgo explicitly per
target rather than relying on Go's root auto-discovery, which would otherwise
apply this amd64 profile to every build including js/wasm:

  - native / novulkan / headless / headless-novulkan / x86-64-v3: `-pgo=$(PGO_PROFILE)`
    (default `default.pgo`; override to point at a target-specific profile).
  - wasm / wasm-profile: `-pgo=$(WASM_PGO)` (default `default.pgo`). PGO input is
    symbolic and applied in the arch-independent inliner, so `default.pgo`'s
    samples for functions shared between the native and wasm builds (bus, IE64
    interpreter, BASIC runtime, video kernels) drive the wasm codegen too;
    amd64-only entries (the native JIT) are dropped and PGO never pessimises, so
    it is >= -pgo=off (measured ~0.2 % wasm size cost). Go cannot sample-profile
    js/wasm directly (no threads/SIGPROF: an IE_CPUPROFILE capture there yields
    zero samples), so covering the wasm JIT paths needs a browser/Node CPU
    capture converted to pprof; set `WASM_PGO=default.wasm.pgo` when one exists,
    or `WASM_PGO=off` to opt out.

## Workloads

| Profile              | Duration | Command                                                                          |
|----------------------|----------|----------------------------------------------------------------------------------|
| compositor_rotozoomer| 30 s     | -ie64 sdk/examples/prebuilt/rotozoomer_ie64.ie64                                   |
| voodoo_megademo      | 30 s     | -ie32 sdk/examples/prebuilt/voodoo_mega_demo.iex                                   |
| audio_wav            | 30 s     | -wav DoctorWhoSID.wav                                                              |
| emutos_desktop       | 35 s     | -emutos -emutos-image sdk/examples/prebuilt/etos256us.img                          |
| iescript_emutos      | 15 s     | -emutos -emutos-image sdk/examples/prebuilt/etos256us.img -script emutos_jit_probe.ies |
| robocop_m68k         | 30 s     | -m68k sdk/examples/prebuilt/robocop_intro_68k.ie68                                 |

The IEScript workload ends when the script calls sys.exit, so its duration is
shorter than the timeout used to bound it.

## Acceptance

`go build -pgo=default.pgo .` completes with no warning and no fallback.

